  "projects": {
    "2018": [
      {
        "title": "Language Server Plugin in Xi",
        "short_description": "Xi-Editor currently has a support of plugins but the Plugin API is quite small. The current plugin API has support for implementing things like...",
        "description": "<p>Xi-Editor currently has a support of plugins but the Plugin API is quite small. The current plugin API has support for implementing things like indentation and syntax check. A lot more useful features can be realized by adding a plugin that supports the Language Server Protocol. It would enable advanced features in the editor like:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Intelligent Autocompletion</li>\n<li>Hover definitions</li>\n<li>Go-to reference and definition of a symbol.</li>\n<li>Highlight references of a symbol</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This project aims at adding Language Server Protocol client plugin to the Xi Editor</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Pranjal Paliwal",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/betterclever/88ca87b3d8809804cadff92b714e4392",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/5127649919762432/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Improve Xi-Mac’s UI and polish its core editing experience",
        "short_description": "Xi-Mac, Xi Editor's official macOS frontend is still very barebones and thus making Xi Editor on Mac not yet fit to act as a developer's main editor....",
        "description": "<p>Xi-Mac, Xi Editor's official macOS frontend is still very barebones and thus making Xi Editor on Mac not yet fit to act as a developer's main editor. This project aims to implement new front end elements to accommodate upcoming features to Xi such as a language server plugin or improving the find and replace functions. Intended elements to implement for this project include a status bar, an autocomplete menu, a view to show definitions, a quick look navigation view, split views and various other improvements to the general feel and aesthetic of the front end to make Xi feel like a native macOS product.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Dũng Lê",
        "code_url": "https://nangtrongvuon.github.io/2018/08/08/my-time-at-gsoc/",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/5576286030266368/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Find Enhancements",
        "short_description": "Searching, finding and replacing text in files is a very common task when working with text editors. Currently, xi-editor only supports a very basic...",
        "description": "<p>Searching, finding and replacing text in files is a very common task when working with text editors. Currently, xi-editor only supports a very basic plain-text search within the currently opened document. Having more advanced search and replace functionality would be very beneficial for all users of xi-editor. In this project I am planning to extend xi-editor to allow search using regular expressions, replacements of matched strings and multiple search queries. Additionally, I intent to integrate a more advanced interface for find and replace into xi-mac as well as highlighting matching text in opened documents.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "scholtzan",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/scholtzan/7668dc065cb02ee45c05447915a05a47",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2018/projects/6281106336776192/"
      }
    ],
    "2019": [
      {
        "title": "High performance piet backend",
        "short_description": "Despite the ubiquity of text in computing applications, rendering high quality text using the GPU remains a challenging problem (see section titled...",
        "description": "<p>Despite the ubiquity of text in computing applications, rendering high quality text using the GPU remains a challenging problem (see section titled Rendering <a href=\"https://hal.inria.fr/hal-01815193/document\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for a brief history). A promising solution was recently proposed by Patrick Walton in the form of a Rust library, <a href=\"http://pcwalton.github.io/2017/02/14/pathfinder.html\" target=\"_blank\">Pathfinder</a>.</p>\n<p>Integrating Pathfinder with piet will enable druid to provide high performance, high quality graphics (using piet), and thus eventually help satisfy Xi’s goal of providing a beautiful yet performant interface, on every platform.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "Brian Merchant",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/bzm3r/10e24f8a544edd17a50897ae29857e51",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2019/projects/4707456339410944/"
      }
    ]
  },
